30457	30561	30454	30454	Rhoda	194	“ What man lives in celibacy ? Consider that unmentionable fact , and then say whether I am wrong in refusing to forgive Miss Royston . Women ’s battle is not only against themselves . The necessity of the case demands what you call a strained ideal . I am seriously convinced that before the female sex can be raised from its low level there will have to be a widespread revolt against sexual instinct . Christianity could n’t spread over the world without help of the ascetic ideal , and this great movement for woman ’s emancipation must also have its ascetics . ”
