121085	121296	121297	121297	Widdowson	218	“ Let me ask myself a question . If Monica were absolutely free to choose between continuing to live with me and resuming her perfect liberty , can I persuade myself that she would remain my wife ? She would not . Not for a day , not for an hour . Of that I am morally convinced . And I acknowledge the grounds of her dissatisfaction . We are unsuited to each other . We do not understand each other . Our marriage is physical and nothing more . My love — what is my love ? I do not love her mind , her intellectual part . If I did , this frightful jealousy from which I suffer would be impossible . My ideal of the wife perfectly suited to me is far liker that girl at the public - house bar than Monica . Monica ’s independence of thought is a perpetual irritation to me . I do n’t know what her thoughts really are , what her intellectual life signifies . And yet I hold her to me with the sternest grasp . If she endeavoured to release herself I should feel capable of killing her . Is not this a strange , a brutal thing ? ”
